{"parentUuid":"191671a1-48ed-4688-acdc-b9dbd002637d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011ATeGhknd3Cb5n2eV6iezB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N7Q1jg5v42fGZpgc1j67Fb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/kanji-stroke-order-svg/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: kanji-stroke-order-svg\ndescription: Generate a standalone textbook-style stroke-order SVG for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke — completed strokes in black, current stroke highlighted with red number and directional arrow, remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill when the user wants ONLY the stroke-order diagram as a raw SVG (no HTML wrapper, no metadata). For the full HTML kanji study sheet with ON/KUN/mnemonic/examples bundled in, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-html` instead.\n---\n\n# Kanji Stroke Order — SVG only\n\nGenerates a single self-contained SVG showing how to write a Japanese character, one stroke at a time, in the canonical order published by KanjiVG (the de facto reference dataset, used by Tagaini Jisho, jisho.org, and most kanji-learning apps).\n\n## When to use\n\nUse this skill when the user wants **just the visual stroke order**, no extra context, no HTML page. Typical triggers:\n\n- \"Give me the stroke-order SVG for 字\"\n- \"Just the diagram for あ, raw SVG\"\n- \"Generate the stroke chart, no template needed\"\n\nFor the richer flow that also embeds ON/KUN readings, mnemonic, examples and example sentence inside a styled HTML page, use `kanji-stroke-order-html` instead.\n\n## How to run\n\nThe script is at `scripts/stroke_diagram.py` and uses only the Python standard library plus an internet connection (it fetches the SVG from the KanjiVG GitHub raw endpoint).\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/stroke_diagram.py <character> -o <output_path>.svg\n```\n\nOptional flags:\n- `--cols N` — max panels per row before wrapping (default 6). For very simple characters (3-4 strokes), pass `--cols 3` or `--cols 4` to keep panels large.\n\n## Output format\n\nA single SVG file. One panel per stroke (109×109 each), laid out left-to-right with automatic row wrapping past 6 panels. In each panel:\n\n- Completed strokes: solid black\n- Current stroke: solid black, slightly thicker\n- Future strokes: light gray (so the final character outline is visible from the first panel, giving the learner a target)\n- Red label at the stroke's starting point: stroke number + arrow (→ ← ↑ ↓) indicating the initial direction of the brush\n\nThe SVG renders correctly in any modern browser.\n\n## Coverage and failure mode\n\nKanjiVG covers:\n- All jōyō kanji (2,136)\n- All jinmeiyō kanji (~860)\n- Hiragana and katakana (full sets)\n- Many additional CJK Unified Ideographs\n\nRare characters from CJK Extensions B–G may not be present. In that case the script exits with a clear error citing the U+ codepoint that was missed.\n\n## Attribution\n\nKanjiVG data is © Ulrich Apel and contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 3.0.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":388837,"output_tokens":1758,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":388837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbUhzVXKsTQHXKaZFTeuS","type":"assistant","uuid":"3bb3cfba-2c18-4a6c-afdf-93c1eba27e88","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:11:34.408Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","ses